{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent upward bias in true outcomes vs model: add a positive level shift. In this sample the model underpredicts by ~+2 to +5 €/t on average, with the gap widening during rallies.",
    "Trend/lag error: when the last 5–10 days show a clear upswing, the model reacts too slowly. Apply a trend-following uplift that increases with recent slope (e.g., proportional to 5–10d momentum).",
    "Horizon-dependent underprediction: errors grow with forecast horizon (weeks 2–4 most). Use an increasing correction with lead time (small in days 1–5, larger by days 15–30).",
    "Rally regime misclassification: during sustained breakouts (price making higher highs), the model mean-reverts too early. Suppress mean-reversion and keep forecasts closer to an extrapolated trend until momentum fades.",
    "Occasional overshoot after late spike signals: when the model finally turns bullish, it can overproject near the far end (e.g., very high last-week forecasts) while true prices flatten/soften. Cap late-horizon upside using a soft ceiling tied to recent realized volatility/resistance (e.g., limit to recent 20d high + k·vol)."
  ]
